Z||000007||Formula88||08-31-2001||09:08 AM||||More information on the show can be had at the Tarheel Tigers GTO Club website: <A HREF="http://www.tarheeltigers.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tarheeltigers.org</A>  .  Click on "Event Dates."<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>September 8th- Raleigh NC- CLUB EVENT Date: Saturday September 8th, 2001. Location: Crown Pontiac Of Raleigh 2501 Capital BLVD Raleigh NC. Time: 9 AM to 4pm. Food, Music and FUN! Dash plaques for the first 100 Cars. Registration: $15, 9AM to 12PM. Judging: 12:30 to 2:30 PM. Awards presentation: 3PM. Award Classes are: Best: Tri Power award. Best: Tempest, Lemans, Firebird, TA, and GTO. Best: Pre-30's, 40's 50's 60's 70's 80's 90's 00, and 2001 Awards. Best: of show to 1976. Best: of show from 1976 to 2001. Special awards given out for: Longest distance driven to show. Hard luck Award. Oldest registered driver award. Youngest registered driver award. Club participation award " registered vehicle " RAIN OR SHINE <BR>Contact Info: ED 919-233-8744, For Pre-Registration FORM E-mail DMMLKM@MINDSPRING.COM <HR></BLOCKQUOTE>||||reg||4
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||08-31-2001||11:29 AM||||Yeah, I figured Fieros would be left out of the judged classes... only shot we'd have is the "Best 80's" trophy.<P>Well, for $15, might be nice to show it off anyway... <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||08-31-2001||12:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>Yeah, I figured Fieros would be left out of the judged classes... only shot we'd have is the "Best 80's" trophy.<P>Well, for $15, might be nice to show it off anyway... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No real surprise here.  It's hosted by a GTO club, so classes for Tempest, Lemans, and GTO make sense (all the same platform), and it would be silly to have ANY Pontiac show without a Firebird/TA class (unless it's only for 1 model).  So, they really only have the variations of those 2 car models. I like the fact that they throw in best of each decade too.  There's no class for Bonneville, Star Chief, Grand Prix, etc. so I don't feel slighted that there's no Fiero class.<P>My goal would be to get a bunch of Fieros to show up, just to remind the "typical" Poncho fan that we're as rabid and fanatical as they are.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||08-31-2001||02:01 PM||||Oh! I didn't realize the Tempest, LeMans and GTO were all 'variations on a theme', so to speak. So yes, that does make a bit more sense. O.K., I don't feel as slighted any more - thanks for pointing me in the right direction. <P>But, yeah, I believe we should get *lots* of Fieros there, but come in one at a time, so they don't even realize we're all from the same group - make them think that the Fiero fan base is even wider than it is.<P>Gonna be fun...||||reg||1
